| Graham Campbell (3 addresses, merged) | 782 | 65.9% | 33 | 80.5% |
| Aiko Tanaka | 206 | 17.4% | 3 | 7.3% |
| root | 117 | 9.9% | 1 | 2.4% |
| Your Name | 69 | 5.8% | 1 | 2.4% |
| Vance Lucas | 10 | 0.8% | 0 | 0.0% |
| StyleCI Bot | 1 | 0.1% | 1 | 2.4% |
| Jonas Staudenmeir | 1 | 0.1% | 1 | 2.4% |
| JT Smith | 1 | 0.1% | 1 | 2.4% |

- **Graham Campbell merge:** It is one guess from names and addresses, and it is not written to `.mailmap`. Unmerged, the figures are:
  - `<email redacted>`: 403 lines (34.0%)
  - `<email redacted>`: 377 lines (31.8%)
  - `<email redacted>`: 2 lines
- **`root` and `Your Name`:** These look like default or placeholder git identities. Check who they are before the audit. Together they hold 15.7% of the lines.
- **Vance Lucas:** Their last commit is from 2015. The 10 lines are credited to them only because of copy detection. With `-w -M` alone they hold 0.
- **Bus factor:** It is 1 with the 3 Graham addresses counted as one person. That person holds 65.9%, and 2 authors reach 80%. Both numbers cover `src/Parser` only. Unmerged, the bus factor is 2 and 3 authors reach 80%. The bus factor is the smallest number of authors whose surviving lines reach 50%. It measures how concentrated the code is, not who understands it.

**`Lexer.php` (58 lines)**
- Graham Campbell holds all 58 lines (100%) with the 2 addresses counted as one person. Unmerged, `<email redacted>` holds 52 lines (89.7%) and the noreply address holds 6 (10.3%).
- The noreply address last committed on 2026-08-24 and is active. The `alt-three.com` address last committed in 2020 and is inactive. Both are the same suspected person, so ask Graham.
- 20 of the 58 lines (34.5%) were moved or copied in from other paths (`src/Loader/Lines.php`, `src/Value.php`, `src/Loader/Value.php`). Credit for those goes to whoever wrote them, not to whoever moved them.
- Copy detection moves a few lines between rows. Without it, Graham's `alt-three.com` address holds 52 of 58 lines with it and 56 without.

**Escape handling**
- `src/Parser/Escape.php` is 206 lines, 100% Aiko Tanaka, in 2 commits. The last commit was 2026-08-26, so they are active.
- Aiko wrote this file recently. The history shows a single author in a short span, so a security audit has less review history to lean on.
- Check `Quirks.php` and `Compat.php` for any escape-related logic. I did not run per-file ownership on them.

**What the numbers leave out**
- **Excluded file:** `src/Parser/Unicode/CharTable.php` is excluded as generated (431 lines). `--keep-generated` would count it.
- **Reformat commits:** No reformat commit was found, so none was ignored.
- **Mechanical rewrites:** I checked 48 commits for them and set aside 0.
- **Bots and `.mailmap`:** The only bot row is StyleCI, with 1 line. There is no `.mailmap` effect on these numbers.
- **Copy detection:** Figures use `-w -M -C`. Copy detection moved 80 lines in 3 files to other authors:

  | Author | With copy detection | Without |
  |---|---|---|
  | Graham Campbell (merged) | 65.9% (782 lines) | 66.7% (792 lines) |
  | Vance Lucas | 0.8% (10 lines) | 0% |

- **What line counts can't show:** They say nothing about code quality, review work, or code deleted on purpose.
